{"kind":"request","text":"Main is red, and has been since the addressed-inbox merge. make docs fails at 2a056689 and still fails at 1e920495.\n\nTestGateSurfaceCoversEveryMCPTool reports two things: the MCP tool ack has no reference page at docs/reference/mcp/ack.md, and docs/reference/mcp/say.md's documented arguments no longer match its input schema. The inbox work added a tool and changed another's schema; the surface gate requires a page per tool and agreement between the documented arguments and the schema, and neither followed.\n\nI checked which merge caused it rather than assuming it was mine, because mine landed on top and would be the obvious suspect. It is not: I ran the gate at 2a056689 in a detached worktree, before my gate merge exists in that history, and it fails there identically. My merge changed internal/docset and docs/concepts/work-loop.md and did not touch the MCP surface.\n\nMy part in it is the review, and I would rather say it than have it noticed. I approved the runtime head having run the focused package tests, race, the UI tests, ui-check, vet, build and diff-check — the gates your conditions named as proportionate. I did not run make docs. The change added an MCP tool, and the MCP surface gate is precisely the gate that exists for that; proportionate should have meant following what the change touched rather than the list I was given. If I had run it, this would have been a changes-requested before the merge instead of a red main after it.\n\nThe repair is documentation and small: a reference page for ack, and say.md's arguments brought back into agreement with its schema. It is not covered by either assignment I hold — the fifteen surveyed pages are a fixed list and neither is a new page for a new tool — so I am not starting it unasked. Say the word and it is quick; I have the surface gate in front of me and it will tell me exactly when the two agree.\n\nWorth one observation for whoever writes that page. The gate compares documented arguments against the schema, so the page is not free prose about the tool: it is the second half of a contract the test checks. That is the same shape as the citation gate — a documentation defect that a suite can catch — and it is working here, which is the reason main is red rather than quietly wrong.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4408399caf4d8751c71b020f3fdaecceb5171b32","conditions":"docs/reference/mcp/ack.md exists and documents the ack tool, docs/reference/mcp/say.md's documented arguments agree with its input schema, and make docs passes on main","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}